{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"5d39974bc52954246699a927d438e9f69e489108ed6cdbfb38315da5cf24fd44","packTokens":5906,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":528,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1043,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":4199,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"A responsive web app for Pulse Studio, a single-location boutique fitness studio offering yoga, pilates, HIIT, spin, and boxing classes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Members browse the weekly class schedule, view class details, book or cancel a spot, join a waitlist when a class is full\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"3 screens: Schedule (home), Class Detail, My Bookings\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Enforce the studio's booking and cancellation rules: capacity, waitlist, 7-day booking window, 15-minute pre-start window, 2-hour cancellation window, no overlaps, 10-booking limit\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Seed data covering current and next week: at least 40 class sessions, 5 instructors, full classes, cancelled classes, demo member with bookings\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Bookings must survive page reload via backend or local persistence\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Design quality as primary criterion: boutique aesthetic, warm off-white background, per-class-type accent colours, dark mode support, WCAG AA contrast\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Full keyboard navigation, screen reader support, semantic structure, 44×44 px touch targets\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Automated tests for business rules and end-to-end test\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Mobile-first responsive from 360 px, tablet 2-column, desktop side panel\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Where does Back go from Class Detail?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Back to the screen Class Detail was opened from (Schedule or My Bookings), keeping that screen's state\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which rules apply when joining a waitlist?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The same 7-day and 15-minute windows plus the past and studio-cancelled rules as booking; overlap and the 10-booking limit are only checked at promotion\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"How does Undo work on the 5-second booking toast?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Undo removes the booking as if it was never made: no cancellation record, no late-cancel warning, counts restored\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"How is the 7-day booking window measured?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Booking is allowed if the class starts within 7×24 hours from now (Europe/London)\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"There is only one real member, so how is waitlist promotion modelled and shown?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Other members exist only as booked and waitlist counts. When Alex cancels, the booked count stays the same and the waitlist count drops by one. Alex's own promotion is triggered by a test/demo hook that simulates another member cancelling\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Are the seed dates fixed calendar dates, or worked out from today's date when the app first loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Worked out from today (Europe/London) on first load, then stored\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a late cancellation ('counts as a missed class') stored differently and shown in Past or the stats?\",\n  \"answer\": \"It is stored as Cancelled with a late flag and shown in Past as 'Late cancel'; stats are unaffected\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Nobody on staff can mark attendance, so what happens to a Booked class once it has finished?\",\n  \"answer\": \"It moves to Past and is shown and counted as Attended automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"The spec has 60 requirements, which is about 5 runs of work. Should it be built in one run, or should part of it be cut or moved to a later run?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve as one run: the request asks for all 3 screens, the rules, the design system and the tests together\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"REQ-33 points to REQ-32 by number, and REQ-58 uses 1023 px as the top of the tablet range. Should either of these be configuration?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep both as fixed values: the REQ-32 reference is a link between requirements, and 1023 px is just the step below the 1024 px desktop breakpoint\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The app must be a responsive single-location booking web app for Pulse Studio offering Yoga, Pilates, HIIT, Spin and Boxing classes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"It must present exactly three screens: Schedule (home at root URL), Class Detail, and My Bookings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"There is a single pre-signed-in member, Alex Rivera, with no sign-in screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"A top bar must show the Pulse Studio wordmark and an avatar with initials AR linking to My Bookings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"All dates, day boundaries and time-based rules must be computed in the Europe/London timezone and times displayed in 24-hour HH:mm format regardless of device timezone or clock setting.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"A seed generator must produce at least 40 class sessions across the five class types and three rooms, five instructors with name, bio and avatar, at least 3 full sessions, at least 3 sessions with 1-3 spots left, at least 1 studio-cancelled session, and for Alex 2 upcoming Booked, 1 Waitlisted and 3 past Attended bookings, none on a cancelled session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"On app load, seed sessions must be generated for the current and next Monday-Sunday week (Europe/London) and stored in local storage if none exists, or existing stored sessions must be reused unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Every booking action must persist bookings, statuses, late flags, session counts and waitlist positions to local storage before reporting success, so data survives a new instance or page reload.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Booking a session with free spots, within the booking window, no overlap, and under the 10-upcoming-booking limit must create a Booked record and increment booked count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Booking or waitlisting a session Alex already holds a record for must be rejected with an 'already booked' error without side effects.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Booking a full session must be rejected with a 'class full' error with counts unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Joining a waitlist on a full, in-window session must create a Waitlisted record with the correct position and increment waitlist count, bypassing overlap and limit checks; joining a waitlist on a non-full session must be rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Booking or waitlisting a session starting more than 168 hours from now must be rejected with an 'outside booking window' error; exactly 168 hours is allowed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Booking or waitlisting a session starting less than 15 minutes from now must be rejected with an 'outside booking window' error; exactly 15 minutes is allowed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Booking, waitlisting, cancelling or leaving a waitlist for a session that has already started must be rejected with a 'class has started' error, leaving data unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Booking or waitlisting a studio-cancelled session must be rejected with a 'cancelled by studio' error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Booking a session that overlaps another Booked session must be rejected with a specific message naming the conflicting class and its time range; sessions touching end-to-start are not considered overlapping.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Booking beyond 10 upcoming Booked sessions must be rejected with a specific limit message; Waitlisted records do not count toward this limit.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling a Booked record for a not-yet-started session must set it to Cancelled with a late flag true only if less than 2 hours remain before start.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling a Booked record must decrement the waitlist count (keeping booked count) if waitlisted members exist, otherwise decrement the booked count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Leaving a waitlist for a not-yet-started session must set the record to Cancelled with late flag false, remove it from Upcoming, and decrement waitlist count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"A test-only hook must promote the first waitlisted member on cancellation: Alex at position 1 becomes Booked if eligible, Alex at higher positions is bumped down by one, and counts are adjusted accordingly.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"If promoting Alex from waitlist position 1 would cause overlap, exceed the 10-booking limit, or violate the 15-minute window, Alex must remain Waitlisted at position 1 with a stored skip reason, and the next member or counts must be adjusted instead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Class Detail must display the stored skip reason next to Alex's waitlist position when applicable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"On app open, if Alex was promoted from waitlist to Booked since the last visit, a one-time toast naming the class must be shown.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Undoing a booking within 5 seconds of the toast must delete the Booked record entirely (no Cancelled record or late flag) and restore the prior booked count.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"A Booked record whose session end time has passed must be returned as Attended in the Past list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"A Booked or Waitlisted record for a session later marked studio-cancelled must appear in the Past list with status 'Cancelled by studio'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The Upcoming list must contain Booked and Waitlisted records for unended sessions, ordered ascending and grouped by day label; the Past list must contain Attended and Cancelled records ordered most recent first.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"My Bookings stats must compute Upcoming count, Classes this month count, and Current streak of consecutive weeks with attendance, unaffected by late cancellations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"A session action state must be computable as Book, Join waitlist, Booked, Waitlisted (with position and skip reason), or Disabled with a reason, following the stated precedence rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"An availability label function must return 'Cancelled', 'Full · N on waitlist', '1 spot left', 'Only N left' (2-3 spots), or 'N spots left' (4+ spots) as appropriate.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"Schedule cards must display the computed availability label per the above rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"A schedule filter function must return a day's sessions, including studio-cancelled ones, ordered by start time, matching any selected type, intensity, and time-of-day filters, with empty filter groups matching everything.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The Schedule screen must show a Monday-Sunday day strip of 7 chips with today highlighted, days without sessions dimmed, and prev/next-week navigation limited to current and next week.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"The Schedule screen must show a filter bar with type, intensity, and time-of-day chips plus a Clear filters action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"Each day's session must be shown as a card with time, duration, name, type tag, intensity, instructor, room, capacity bar with label, and an action button, with cancelled sessions struck through.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The action button on each card must read Book, Join waitlist, Booked ✓, or Waitlisted #N, or be disabled for started, cancelled, or out-of-window sessions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"Activating a schedule card outside its button (or a My Bookings row) must open Class Detail for that session without creating a booking.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"Booking from a Schedule card must update the card immediately and show a toast with an Undo action available for 5 seconds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"Joining/leaving a waitlist or cancelling a booking must show a confirmation toast with no Undo action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"If an optimistic booking action is rejected or fails, the UI must revert to its previous state and show a plain-language error toast with no raw error or stack trace.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"The Schedule screen must show skeleton cards while loading, an empty-day message, a no-filter-match message with Clear filters, or an inline error with Retry, as appropriate.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"Using Back from Class Detail must return to the originating screen with its prior day, week, filter and tab state preserved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"Class Detail must show a hero header with accent colour, class info, timing, room, instructor card, description, what-to-bring list, availability block, and the free-cancellation text.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The Class Detail footer must show the correct action/status text per booking state, stay pinned at the bottom on small viewports, and reflect disabled reasons as appropriate.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling from Class Detail or My Bookings must open a confirmation dialog, showing a late-cancellation warning when under 2 hours remain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"A rejected booking attempt from Class Detail must show the rule's error message and, if due to the class becoming full, refresh availability and switch the footer to Join waitlist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"My Bookings must show a header, three stat tiles, Upcoming/Past tabs, with Upcoming rows grouped by day showing badges and actions, and Past rows showing status badges.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"My Bookings must show empty-state and loading/error messages for no-upcoming, no-past, loading, and failed states, respectively.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"The app must use defined colour design tokens including background, text, semantic colours, and per-class-type accent colours applied consistently.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"The app must support a dark theme matching the system preference, meeting contrast requirements.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"The app must use defined display and body fonts, a type scale, and tabular figures for numbers/times.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The app must replace animations with instant changes when reduced motion is preferred.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"All interactive elements must be reachable and operable via keyboard with visible focus indicators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The app must use semantic markup, accessible capacity bar announcements, and pair colour signals with text or icons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"Dialogs must trap focus, close on Escape, and return focus to the triggering control.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The app must avoid horizontal scrolling at narrow widths, use a 2-column card layout at tablet widths, and show Class Detail as a side panel at desktop widths.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"All interactive targets must be at least 44x44 px.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"Automated unit tests must cover the core booking business rules and pass in CI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"An automated end-to-end test must cover the schedule-to-booking-to-cancel flow and pass in CI.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"When loaded data does not cover the current/next week, the service must generate missing weeks' sessions across all class types without altering existing bookings, sessions, or counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling a non-Booked record or leaving a waitlist on a non-Waitlisted record must be rejected with an 'invalid booking state' error, leaving all data unchanged.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}